# Reference — TA Weapons

Every weapon the v3.1c install loads, cross-referenced with each unit's
`Weapon1/2/3=` fields. **{{.TotalWeapons}} weapon definitions**, used
(collectively) by **{{.UnitsWithWeapon}} units** (and some unused / fired
only by other weapons).

The game reads weapons only from the `.tdf` files directly in
`weapons/` (`gamedata/weapons.tdf` is not a weapon source) and places
each section in a 256-slot table at the slot its `ID=` names: a section
without an ID is not loaded, and a later section with the same ID
replaces an earlier one. Each row's `Key` is the section name; a unit's
`Weapon1=` / `Weapon2=` / `Weapon3=` finds the lowest slot whose `Key`
matches, ignoring case. `ID` is that slot. `Range` is the value the
game uses (32767 when the key is missing). Archetype tokens come from
the boolean weapon flags (`ballistic`, `lineofsight`, `dropped`,
`beamweapon`, `guidance`, `selfprop`, `twophase`, `burnblow`,
`waterweapon`, `noexplode`).

See the kbot docs for column semantics:

- [TDF: weapon TDFs](https://github.com/coreprime/kbot/blob/main/docs/formats/tdf.md#tdf--feature-weapon-sound-definitions)
  — what each `weapons/*.tdf` field controls.
- [Gamedata: weapons.tdf reference](https://github.com/coreprime/kbot/blob/main/docs/formats/gamedata.md#weaponstdf--weapon-tdf-reference)
  — the engine's full weapon-field catalogue.
- [TA vs TA:K formats matrix](https://github.com/coreprime/kbot/blob/main/docs/formats/compare.md)
  — how TA's separate `weapons/*.tdf` model differs from TA:K's inline
  `[WEAPONn]` model.

> [!NOTE]
> **Not every unit-cited weapon name resolves to a definition here.**
> A name that matches no loaded weapon gives the unit no weapon in that
> slot; such names are marked `—` in the *Defined?* column of the
> cross-reference below.

